  "final_message": "If you don't pass `max_attempts`, `call_with_retry()` makes at most **4** attempts, and that count includes the first try.\n\n- **The default:** In `retry.py`, `DEFAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 4`. When `max_attempts` is `None`, the function uses that value.\n- **How the limit works:** It loops with `for _ in range(attempts)`, so it calls `fn()` exactly 4 times. It returns as soon as a call succeeds; if all 4 fail, it raises the last exception.\n- **The other constants don't apply:** `decoy_network.py` has `MAX_RETRIES = 3` and `decoy_backoff.py` has `RETRY_LIMIT = 5`, but `retry.py` never imports either one.\n- **Other files:** `main7.py` just calls `call_with_retry(lambda: 1)` with no `max_attempts`. `.amplifier/settings.local.yaml` has nothing to do with retries.\n\nANSWER: 4",
